    "body": "Owner's answers on the program start (Sodick AQ600L, LN2W, 2026-11-25), resolving the held `G0 Z0` question:\n\n- The work offset is set at the control at X0 Y0, and the operator sets the upper head at the correct height above the part: that height is **Z0**.\n- The post should **always rapid to Z0 at the start, after the initial X Y positioning and before `T91`**.\n- The **first line must zero the U V axes** (taper axes back to vertical).\n\nOwner's example of the start of a cut (his own description of what the control expects; the Z0 and U V lines go before it):\n```\nG00 X-22. Y10.\nT91\nT84\nT94\nC000\nG01 X-25.838 Y10.\nG03 X-18.167 Y9.808 I3.838 J0\n```\n\nSo the LN2W start order is: zero U V → `G00` to the start X Y → `G00 Z0` → `T91` thread → `T84` → `T94` → `C…` → cut. No `G21`. Still to confirm with the owner: the exact form of the U V zero line (e.g. `G00 U0 V0`). The `G0 Z0` start move moves into scope of this issue.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
